# Line-ending policy for the validation suite.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The requirements baseline is protected by a SHA-256 taken over its RAW BYTES
# (validators/baseline_guard.py). Git's autocrlf would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes those bytes and would make every fresh clone on Windows report
# REQUIREMENTS_BASELINE_MODIFIED even though nobody had touched the requirements.
#
# A false alarm on that control is worse than no control - people learn to ignore it.
# So line endings are pinned here, and the baseline itself is exempted from any
# conversion at all.
#
# This file sits inside requirements_validation_tests/ rather than at the repository
# root: gitattributes apply to their own subtree, and the root belongs to the CredPilot
# implementation, not to the QA layer.

# Normalise the suite's text files to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The hashed baseline: never convert, byte-for-byte as committed.
source_requirements/requirements_verbatim.md -text

# The source document and its page images are binary evidence - never touch them.
*.docx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.jpg   binary
